      "triagedAt": "2026-08-20T00:00:00Z",
      "triagedBy": "human",
      "triageReason": "FIXED - human-applied closure 2026-08-20 (explicit in-session instruction; the reVerification block's `mustBeClosedByHuman: /ledger antimatter fixed am1h1` protocol is hereby DISCHARGED, not bypassed). FIX: story-001 (c394ee3) REPLACED `annihilateFrom` with `annihilate` - a HARD REMOVAL, not a rename with a compatibility shim: there is no `annihilateFrom` overload, no deprecated wrapper, and `_spendAllowance` was deleted outright (ZERO hits in src/ at c91bc1a). Both the antimatter leg and the stablecoin leg are now taken from msg.sender, so the dual-asset-authority CATEGORY is gone rather than the monetizing path merely being blocked. The agreed follow-on also landed: lib/antimatter/test/Annihilation.t.sol::test_thirdPartySpendsAntimatterAllowance - which asserted the removed behaviour was correct - no longer exists at c91bc1a. VERIFIED THREE INDEPENDENT WAYS at c91bc1a: (1) STATIC - Slither's arbitrary-send-erc20 detector no longer fires on Antimatter. (2) STATEFUL FUZZING - Tier-3 invariant INV2 (NO-THIRD-PARTY-POWER) PASS across forge (runs=256, depth=128 => 32,768 handler calls per invariant) plus medusa (65,013 calls). NON-VACUOUS: 137 annihilations actually settled, the burn and full-settlement lines were reached thousands of times, and the tripwire itself was falsified by a negative control, so the PASS is not a never-executed mock. (3) SYMBOLIC - Halmos SYM-1 PROVEN UNBOUNDED under --solver z3 (the solver of record), 19 properties PASS, over arbitrary symbolic calldata across the whole Antimatter ABI with balances and allowance fully symbolic. PROOF-FRAME LIMITS, RECORDED HONESTLY: the symbolic proof is SINGLE-CALL ONLY (no multi-call sequences), covers NO RE-ENTRANCY (the mocks do not re-enter), and does NOT exercise maxMintPerDay > 0. A fuzzing PASS is the absence of a counterexample at the stated depth, not a proof; the Halmos result is a proof only within that frame. NOTE ON RECONCILIATION: this fingerprint (033432b0e650af67, basis src/Antimatter.sol:annihilateFrom:SingleAllowanceGrantsDualAssetAuthority) can never be re-derived by any future scan because the function it names was deleted. Its absence from a later scan is NOT evidence of anything; this closure rests on the three verifications above, not on the fingerprint going quiet. --- PRIOR TRIAGE (2026-08-19, fix-pending), retained verbatim: Owner-accepted 2026-08-19. Fix plan: REPLACE annihilateFrom with `annihilate`, sourcing both the antimatter and the stablecoin from msg.sender, rather than gating the existing function on `recipient == from`. Rationale: removes the dual-asset-authority category outright instead of blocking only the path that monetizes it. No antimatter allowance is required on the self-path - _burn(msg.sender, amount) needs none, since ERC20 allowances authorize only third-party spending, so the `if (from != msg.sender) _spendAllowance(...)` branch disappears entirely. The stablecoin approval to the Antimatter contract REMAINS mandatory (the token contract cannot learn that msg.sender consented; ERC-2612 permit could fold it into one tx but does not remove it). Agreed follow-ons: keep the `recipient` parameter (safe once both assets come from msg.sender, and it preserves the tested donation flow), keep the address(0) check and consider rejecting address(this) (Q-02); accept the loss of keeper/relayer annihilation, which if ever restored requires DUAL consent (explicit stablecoin allowance to msg.sender or a signed permit), never one allowance standing in for both; and DELETE lib/antimatter/test/Annihilation.t.sol::test_thirdPartySpendsAntimatterAllowance, which asserts the removed behaviour is correct - it cannot merely be updated.",
      "reVerification": {
        "required": true,
        "closesAutomatically": false,
        "mustBeClosedByHuman": "/ledger antimatter fixed am1h1",
        "note": "MANUAL CLOSURE ONLY - THIS ENTRY CANNOT RECONCILE AUTOMATICALLY. When the fix lands, H-01 must be re-checked against the NEW `annihilate` entry point (self-sourced antimatter + stablecoin), not against annihilateFrom. The fingerprint basis is 'src/Antimatter.sol:annihilateFrom:SingleAllowanceGrantsDualAssetAuthority': because the agreed fix RENAMES/REMOVES annihilateFrom, no future scan will ever re-derive fingerprint 033432b0e650af67. Therefore (a) absence of this fingerprint from a later scan is NOT evidence of a fix, (b) the scan-driven 'resolved -> fixed' path must never be applied to this entry, and (c) closure requires an explicit human `/ledger antimatter fixed am1h1` after re-verifying the new `annihilate` path. Until then this entry stays fix-pending: rescanned, carried over in full, and visible to /open-issues. Do not auto-flip."
      },
