        "auditAuthoredNote": "AUDIT-AUTHORED proof-of-concept written for this audit under workspace/antimatter/test/audit/. It is NOT part of the antimatter project's own test suite, is not present in the submodule at any commit, and must never be cited as project coverage nor filed as a project test path."
      },
      "triagedAt": "2026-08-20T00:00:00Z",
      "triagedBy": "human",
      "triageReason": "FIXED - human-applied closure 2026-08-20, BOUNDARY-SCOPED (WATCH-02-03 qualification stated as required). FIX: story-002 (f48f30d) closes the vector AT THE ANTIMATTER BOUNDARY - toStableAmount now cross-checks the minter's registered decimals against the token's own decimals(), read by RAW STATICCALL (not try/catch, so a return-data decode failure and a codeless token both fail closed), and reverts DecimalsMismatch on ANY disagreement IN BOTH DIRECTIONS (Antimatter.sol:292-295 at c91bc1a). VERIFIED at c91bc1a: (1) STATEFUL FUZZING - Tier-3 INV6 (DECIMALS-CROSSCHECK) PASS; the exact run-01 exploit (register an 18-decimal token as 6 decimals, pay 1e-10 of a token, receive 200 phUSD) now reverts DecimalsMismatch BEFORE the burn - 52 understated and 50 overstated attempts, 0 settled. (2) SYMBOLIC - Halmos SYM-2 PROVEN, 32 properties PASS, with `amount` and the decimals() answer word unbounded. *** BOUNDARY-SCOPED - THIS CLOSURE COVERS THE ANTIMATTER PATH ONLY (WATCH-02-03, BINDING). *** PhusdStableMinter.mint(address,uint256) REMAINS PERMISSIONLESSLY MIS-SCALABLE: the root cause lives in PhusdStableMinter.calculateMintAmount at PhusdStableMinter.sol:254, inside a NESTED DEPENDENCY, and is reachable DIRECTLY without passing through Antimatter at all. That residual is NOT closed by this entry and is tracked separately as the cross-boundary item CODE-205 / MR-02-P3. Closing am1m1 must never be read as closing the underlying minter defect. PROOF-FRAME CAVEATS, RECORDED HONESTLY: (a) SYM-2 enumerated `d` (registered decimals) CONCRETELY over 0..18 because halmos 0.3.3 over-approximates 10**(symbolic); 0..18 is nonetheless THE COMPLETE REACHABLE DOMAIN, since d > 18 is proven separately AND symbolically to revert UnsupportedDecimals - so the enumeration is exhaustive over reachable states, not a sample. (b) The decimals() RETURNDATA LENGTH was enumerated over {revert, 0, 31, 32, 33, 64} with content symbolic - THAT IS AN ENUMERATION, NOT A PROOF over all lengths, and must be cited as such. (c) INV6 does NOT cover a token that LIES CONSISTENTLY to both the staticcall and the registration - a cross-check between two values from the same lying source cannot detect agreement-in-error. --- PRIOR TRIAGE (2026-08-19, fix-pending), retained verbatim: Owner will fix: cross-check the registered `decimals` against IERC20Metadata(stable).decimals() in toStableAmount and revert on mismatch. Verified 2026-08-19 against mainnet @ block 25788032 that all 26 major stablecoins checked (USDC, USDT, DAI, USDS, DOLA, USDe, sUSDe, FRAX, crvUSD, GHO, LUSD, PYUSD, TUSD, USDP, BUSD, FDUSD, deUSD, mkUSD, RLUSD, USDY, EURC, GUSD, sDAI, sUSDS, USDA, alUSD) do implement decimals(), so the catch/revert-on-unavailable leg excludes no real stablecoin. Two implementation notes for the fix: (1) USDT declares `decimals` as uint256 — a uint8-typed call still decodes correctly (raw word 0x..06), so IERC20Metadata is safe; (2) Solidity's try/catch does NOT catch the extcodesize check, so a codeless `stable` reverts bare rather than with DecimalsUnavailable — use a raw staticcall with a returndata length check if the named error must be the actual outcome.",
