          "dEnumerationIsComplete": "`d` (the registered decimals) is ENUMERATED CONCRETELY over 0..18 because halmos 0.3.3 over-approximates `10 ** symbolic` as uninterpreted (probe check_sym2_probe_symbolicExpIsConcrete; --smt-exp-by-const 19 does not help). 0..18 IS THE COMPLETE REACHABLE DOMAIN: d > 18 is proven separately AND SYMBOLICALLY to revert UnsupportedDecimals (check_sym2_registeredAbove18_unreachable, d symbolic over 19..255). The enumeration is therefore exhaustive over reachable states, not a sample.",
          "returndataLengthIsAnEnumerationNotAProof": "THE decimals() RETURNDATA LENGTH IS ENUMERATED over {revert, 0, 31, 32, 33, 64}, with returndata CONTENT symbolic. THIS IS AN ENUMERATION, NOT A PROOF over all lengths. Label it as such wherever it is cited.",
          "keyResults": [
