      "recheckInstruction": "RE-CHECK INSTRUCTION (corrected): read the DEPLOYED yield strategy - resolved from chain for the stablecoins actually registered - and measure creditedPrincipal versus amount there. DO NOT re-check the phUSD-stable-minter pin: it is already current (d6ed1156 == remote master tip) and re-checking it would wrongly conclude that this park is resolved. The open question is the deployed strategy/vault version, not the minter's. If the deployed strategy's deposit() returns no value or credits the full principal (043ff2c-era behaviour), close as not-applicable. If it credits less than the principal transferred, size the stable leg from the returned value (minter-side fix) and/or have Antimatter assert mintedForStable is within tolerance of minter.calculateMintAmount(stable, stableAmount).",
