      "severityDowngrade_2026_08_20": {
        "decision": "HUMAN-AUTHORISED DOWNGRADE, severity low -> qa. STATUS REMAINS open. THIS IS A DOWNGRADE, NOT A CLOSURE - the doNotClose marker in impactInversion_antimatter_02 REMAINS BINDING.",
        "authorisedBy": "human, in-session 2026-08-20, with stated reasoning. RECORDED, NOT RE-LITIGATED.",
        "reason": "NO PERMISSIONLESS VECTOR. The run-02 re-wording ('griefing brick') OVERSTATED the finding by implying an arbitrary attacker; it does not.",
        "mechanismStillReal": "The window between the phUSDBefore snapshot (src/Antimatter.sol:244) and the delta read (:256) DOES contain three external calls - safeTransferFrom (:246), forceApprove (:247) and minter.mint (:251, which itself reaches the yield strategy) - so control genuinely leaves the contract. NO hook on Antimatter and NO re-entry is required. `nonReentrant` guards RE-ENTRY into `annihilate`; it does NOT stop a callee making an OUTBOUND phUSD.transfer(antimatter, 1) while it holds control. The mechanism is demonstrable: the invariant harness reproduced PhUSDAmountMismatch(100e18, 100e18+1).",
        "whyNotLow": "EXACTLY THREE ACTORS get execution inside that window - the `stable` token, the minter, and the yield strategy - and ALL THREE ARE OWNER-CONFIGURED. An unprivileged attacker gets NO execution at all: a donation BEFORE the call is baselined out by the :244 snapshot, and a donation AFTER :256 is irrelevant. No front-run or sandwich reaches inside the interval.",
        "law3Framing": "Therefore this is a LAW-3 FOOTGUN CONDITIONAL ON A HOSTILE OR BUGGY REGISTERED TOKEN. A token with that power can brick its own pair far more cheaply by simply reverting transferFrom - the MARGINAL-CAPABILITY DEFLATOR already applied to L-04.",
        "supersedes": "The run-02 'GRIEFING BRICK' impact wording in impactInversion_antimatter_02.impactINVERTED.nowIs, insofar as it implies an arbitrary third party. That block is RETAINED VERBATIM as history; this correction is APPENDED, not substituted into it.",
        "survivingSubstanceAtQaBand": {
          "rootCauseUNCHANGED": "STILL OPEN. `mintedForStable` at :256 is an UNATTRIBUTED BALANCE DELTA, not 'what the minter minted for this call'. The downgrade does not touch the root cause.",
          "recommendation": "`mintedForStable < expectedForStable` is STRICTLY BETTER than `!=` - it catches a SHORT MINT without turning an OVER-ARRIVAL into a brick.",
          "underflowSibling": "A mid-call phUSD DEPARTURE underflows the :256 subtraction into a bare Panic(0x11) rather than a named error. Same reachability caveat as above (owner-configured actors only)."
        },
        "doNotClose": "BINDING AND UNCHANGED. A downgrade is not a closure. Do not mark this fixed on the strength of the :257 check."
      },
      "triagedAt": "2026-08-20T00:00:00Z",
      "triagedBy": "human",
      "triageReason": "SEVERITY DOWNGRADE low -> qa, human-applied 2026-08-20 (explicit in-session instruction with stated reasoning; recorded, not re-litigated). STATUS DELIBERATELY LEFT open. Basis: NO PERMISSIONLESS VECTOR. Control does leave the contract inside the [:244, :256] window - safeTransferFrom (:246), forceApprove (:247) and minter.mint (:251, reaching the yield strategy) - so no hook on Antimatter and no re-entry is required, and nonReentrant does not stop an OUTBOUND phUSD.transfer(antimatter, 1) from a callee holding control (harness reproduced PhUSDAmountMismatch(100e18, 100e18+1)). BUT the only three actors with execution in that window - the stable token, the minter and the yield strategy - are ALL OWNER-CONFIGURED; an unprivileged attacker gets no execution at all (a pre-call donation is baselined out by the :244 snapshot, a post-:256 donation is irrelevant, and no front-run or sandwich reaches inside the interval). So this is a Law-3 footgun conditional on a hostile or buggy registered token, and such a token can brick its own pair far more cheaply by simply reverting transferFrom (the marginal-capability deflator already applied to L-04). The run-02 'griefing brick' wording overstated it by implying an arbitrary attacker. SURVIVING SUBSTANCE RETAINED AT QA BAND (see severityDowngrade_2026_08_20.survivingSubstanceAtQaBand): the unattributed balance delta at :256 is UNCHANGED and STILL OPEN; the recommendation `mintedForStable < expectedForStable` is strictly better than `!=`; and the Panic(0x11) underflow sibling on a mid-call phUSD departure stands with the same reachability caveat. THE doNotClose MARKER REMAINS BINDING - THIS IS A DOWNGRADE, NOT A CLOSURE. --- PRIOR TRIAGE: none recorded (entry was untriaged/open from antimatter-01 through antimatter-02). Prior analysis blocks titleHistory and impactInversion_antimatter_02 are RETAINED VERBATIM above, unmodified.",
