      "poc": null,
      "run02Observation": "STILL OPEN AND STILL LIVE at c91bc1a. The new :257 equality check re-quotes at the post-inclusion rate on BOTH sides, so it binds nothing the caller saw at signing time and there is still no caller-supplied minimum-output parameter anywhere in annihilate. Reconciles to this entry; not re-filed. See watchItems (WATCH-02-02) - closure explicitly NOT proposed.",
      "watchItems": [
        {
          "id": "WATCH-02-02",
          "raisedAtRun": "antimatter-02",
          "title": "F-01 FALSE-CLOSURE WATCH - HIGHEST-PROBABILITY FALSE CLOSURE IN THIS DELTA",
          "instruction": "c91bc1a implements this finding's own recommended mitigation TEXT verbatim while leaving its DEFECT intact. Any future run proposing 3aac91383dcb6060 fixed on the strength of the :234/:257 exact-equality pair must be REJECTED. Closure requires evidence of a CALLER-SUPPLIED minimum-output parameter (e.g. `uint256 minPhUSDOut` checked as `amount + mintedForStable >= minPhUSDOut` before :260).",
          "counterEvidenceFiledThisRun": "Q-05 (1b960956475d434a), whose falseClosureBlock carries the required attestation.",
          "alsoNote": "This fingerprint is FINGERPRINT-DRIFT-AFFECTED and was MISSING from the deduplicator's drift list. Never re-derive it from c91bc1a source."
        }
      ],
      "triagedAt": "2026-08-21T00:00:00Z",
      "triagedBy": "human",
      "triageReason": "FIX-PENDING - owner-accepted 2026-08-21 (in-session instruction). The defect is CONFIRMED VALID and a fix is OWED; this entry is therefore NEVER suppressed - it is rescanned, carried over and shown by /open-issues until a human marks it fixed. AGREED FIX: add a caller-supplied `uint256 minPhUSDOut` parameter to `annihilate` and check the caller's TOTAL receipt against it, i.e. `if (amount + mintedForStable < minPhUSDOut) revert ...` before settlement. This satisfies WATCH-02-02's closure bar (a CALLER-SUPPLIED minimum-output parameter) exactly. SIMPLIFICATION ACCEPTED BY THE OWNER: the pre-burn quote `expectedForStable = minter.calculateMintAmount(...)` and its zero check `if (expectedForStable == 0) revert PhUSDNotReceived();` are BOTH REMOVED, along with the post-mint exact-equality check `if (mintedForStable != expectedForStable) revert PhUSDAmountMismatch(...)`. Rationale (owner): the caller's own minimum is the real protection, so re-deriving the minter's quote inside annihilate is redundant calculation. The audit agrees the zero check carries no state risk once removed - it was a fail-fast BEFORE the irreversible burn, and a post-burn revert unwinds the whole transaction anyway, so its only value was gas.",
      "fixPlan_2026_08_21": {
        "acceptedBy": "human, in-session 2026-08-21",
        "shape": "add `uint256 minPhUSDOut` to annihilate; compare `amount + mintedForStable` against it; delete the expectedForStable quote, the PhUSDNotReceived zero check and the PhUSDAmountMismatch equality check.",
        "satisfiesWatch": "WATCH-02-02. The bar is a CALLER-SUPPLIED minimum-output parameter; this is one. On landing, F-01 may be proposed fixed - but closure still requires a human /ledger antimatter fixed am1f1 after verifying the parameter is present, is checked against amount + mintedForStable, and is checked BEFORE settlement.",
        "knownConsequencesToVerifyWhenItLANDS": [
          "L-01 (ad4b779566291190) IMPACT RE-INVERTS. The exact-equality check at :257 is currently the ONLY thing that catches mid-call phUSD injection; removing it restores the ORIGINAL run-01 behaviour, in which phUSD arriving in the window [phUSDBefore snapshot, delta read] is FORWARDED to the caller-chosen recipient via safeTransfer(recipient, mintedForStable). Injection RAISES mintedForStable, so it passes a minimum-output check by construction and cannot be caught by it. L-01 therefore reverts from availability-brick back to VALUE LEAK (its run-01 framing, PoC: 500e18 injected, annihilator received 700e18). L-01 STAYS OPEN across this change - the root cause never moved - but its severityHistory and impact wording must be updated again, and the 2026-08-20 QA downgrade (reasoned on 'no permissionless vector' for the BRICK) must be RE-EXAMINED against the leak framing, not carried over unread.",
          "Q-05 (1b960956475d434a) BECOMES MOOT BY DELETION, NOT BY ARGUMENT. Q-05 is a defect in the comment at :232-233 and the PhUSDAmountMismatch error name; this fix deletes both. When it lands, Q-05 may be proposed fixed on the grounds that the misleading text no longer exists. Its reweighCondition (re-weigh to LOW if F-01 is closed or this guard is cited as closing it) is DISCHARGED rather than triggered, because F-01 is being closed by a genuine minimum-output parameter and NOT by citing the equality check.",
          "L-03 (0ed1c6e3270816c5) MECHANISM CHANGES. Its stated brick is 'the stable leg rounds to zero and PhUSDNotReceived kills the whole annihilation'. PhUSDNotReceived is being deleted, so a near-zero exchangeRate no longer reverts there; it instead yields mintedForStable ~ 0, which reverts only if the CALLER set minPhUSDOut above `amount`. The finding is not fixed - it becomes caller-visible slippage rather than an unconditional revert - but its title and mechanism need rewriting on the next run. Do NOT auto-close it on the disappearance of PhUSDNotReceived.",
          "NEW FOOTGUN TO ASSESS: with the zero check gone, a caller (or an integrator whose ABI defaults the new parameter to 0) who passes minPhUSDOut = 0 opts out of the stable-leg guarantee entirely - the stablecoin is pulled and deposited, and a zero stable-leg mint settles with the caller receiving only the antimatter leg. This is the ordinary cost of a slippage parameter, but it is new surface introduced by this fix and should be scanned for at the next run rather than assumed benign.",
          "LAW-2 / F-04 REPEAT RISK: this change rewrites the settlement post-condition a second time. F-04 (d34180996ba41ff8) is open precisely because the FIRST such rewrite arrived untagged while story-001's checklist still self-certified the settlement assertions as preserved unchanged. Land this one under a story (new story-003, or an amendment to 002) so the same provenance gap is not re-opened."
        ]
      },
