      "title": "RECOVERABILITY IS NOW LOAD-BEARING AND IS UNVERIFIED IN THIS PROJECT",
      "instruction": "The owner's stated posture trades brick-PREVENTION for brick-RECOVERY: 'if funds are stuck for whatever reason, we must be able to always migrate away', with that responsibility sited in the DOWNSTREAM STAKER rather than in antimatter. Two consequences follow and must not be lost. (1) The acknowledgements of L-04 and L-05 REST ON A PROPERTY THIS AUDIT HAS NOT VERIFIED - no run of this project has established that a staker holding a position against a bricked antimatter pair can in fact migrate away, nor that the migrate path is itself immune to the same brick. The property lives outside lib/antimatter, so it cannot be checked from an antimatter scan; it must be checked where the staker lives. (2) This posture RAISES the weight of the two open centralization entries rather than lowering it: C-01 (2a844d32db2eb0f9 - FlaxToken.revokeAllMintPrivileges silently voids every outstanding claim and Antimatter exposes NO VIEW of its own authorisation status) and C-02 (3a90280bed325637 - Antimatter has no kill switch of its own). Under a prevention posture those are hygiene; under a recovery posture they are RECOVERY INSTRUMENTS - you cannot execute a recovery you cannot observe the need for, and cannot halt the path you are recovering from. Neither is being acknowledged here; both stay OPEN and should be re-weighed against this posture at the next run.",
